  {
   "id": "R1",
   "severity": "low",
   "locator": "note L1",
   "summary": "pg_ctl's shell command uses /C without /D (pg_ctl.c:556-561) and its postgres -V probe runs via pgwin32_popen/_popen (pg_ctl.c:952; exec.c:330,360; port.h:365-368; system.c:108); Microsoft cmd docs: without /d HKLM/HKCU Command Processor AutoRun executes first; can alter postmaster environment and spawn children; not fail-closed",
   "repair": "Detect-only existence check of both AutoRun values with its own grant; present/unavailable blocks; no value text emitted; never modify; pin System32 cmd.exe or also check Wow6432Node"
  },
  {
   "id": "R2",
   "severity": "low",
   "locator": "note M2 retained-handle/creation-ordering text",
   "summary": "Microsoft documents PID validity only until termination, not non-reuse while a handle is open; PROCESSENTRY32W parent is a PID; lower-bound ordering alone does not exclude post-exit PID reuse; version-probe shell makes downward search ambiguous",
   "repair": "GetProcessTimes containment on retained handles (shell created within pg_ctl lifetime; postmaster created after shell while shell running) and upward walk from pidfile PID"
  },
  {
   "id": "R3",
   "severity": "low",
   "locator": "note M2 SQL confirmation",
   "summary": "SQL session tied to bound postmaster only by time intervals and data-directory lock; Windows PostgreSQL sets no address-reuse option (pqcomm.c:550-582) so port exclusivity is not a basis",
   "repair": "Mandatory direct link: pg_backend_pid() parent equals bound postmaster under R2 predicate, or listener owner PID equals bound postmaster; times supporting only"
  }
 ],
 "informational": [
  "I1 QueryInformationJobObject(NULL) reports only the immediate job when nested; start only outside any job unless all enclosing policies established",
  "I2 pidfile line 7 empty on Windows (pidfile.h; win32_shmem.c none); line 2 spelling under N4 without normalization",
  "I3 PgStartTime set once (postmaster.c:1372); crash-restart detection relies on same-connection B failing",
  "I4 session/local preload settings are per-session evidence",
  "I5 Toolhelp reads all process names in memory; upward handle walk minimizes unrelated reads"
 ],
